{
 "id": "District",
 "notes": [
  "Set metres: the main tower's front column line is Y = 0 (its face looks out along -Y), X runs along that face with column C1 at X = 0, Z up from the tower's foot.",
  "Measured on the Breakout shot (calibration/stereo.py, orthophoto.py) in solve units of 11 m: bays 0.747 (8.2 m), storeys 0.38 (4.18 m), columns 0.08 square; she breaks out of storey 18 through the bay left of C1.",
  "The sky's cumulus are solid (CIN.Clouds.Field), bases 600 m up all round the district; crows (CIN.Birds.Flock) wheel round the tower where she breaks out and wider over the district.",
  "The tower is 26 storeys under its roof (108.7 m): Breakout's camera sees its face up to 95 m, never its top; the hand shot sees the roof edge at the lower left.",
  "Round the tower stands the district's high-rise (CIN.City.Field, blocks 45-140 m, clear within 72 m of the tower) and, past its right end along its face, the skeletal Annex: Breakout's frame 180 sees its top 114 m up some 80 m away (its storeys 65 px apart) and everything else in the picture above 76 m.  The breach throws dust (Breach Dust, from frame 96, rolling along the face towards +X and down: Breakout's camera hovers 4 m in front of the breach the whole shot and the reference keeps the dust at the left of the picture, off the lens) and debris (Breach Debris, Falling Debris); dust fills the storey behind the glass before it (Room Dust).",
  "The district's air is hazy low down (CIN.Air: 0.0025 per metre at the ground, thinning to 1/e every 140 m): Breakout's far towers fade, the hand shot's sky overhead stays clear.",
  "Above the breach storey the tower is its front frame alone (Tower Crown, storeys 19-26: columns, edge beams and braces, no floors, no mullions, roof 108.7 m up): from frame 116 on the reference shows sky through big braces over her, while the breach storey keeps its mullions and the floor over it (frames 76-92).",
  "What the breach throws into the air is shown only while Breakout looks at it (frames up to 206): the hand shot that cuts in at 207 shows clear sky and crows.",
  "Round her after the breach (the hand and flight shots, frames 200-379) a flock wheels close by (Crows Round: headings all round, 2-20 m from her), as the reference's crows cross the lens.",
  "Inside the tower's frame below its crown stands its dark core (Tower Core, set 2.5 m back from the face): the reference sees a dark interior through the facade (frames 76-92), never the sky through the building.",
  "The bay she breaks out through (storey 18, between x -8.2 and 0.0) is left open in the tower and stands as a panel of its own (Breach Panel: its braces and mullions, inside ghosts of the tower's own column and beams) until the frame before she breaks it (95); its pieces are the Breach Debris."
 ],
